Senior DevOps / SRE Interview – Stripe


Round 1 – System Design & Architecture (45 min)

• Design a system that handles sudden traffic spikes. Where do you protect the system?
• How do you design backpressure in a microservices architecture?
• What happens when your rate limiting is misconfigured under heavy load?
• How do you prevent cascading failures between services?
• How would you design idempotent APIs in distributed systems?

⸻

Round 2 – Production Failures (60 min)

• Your system starts timing out intermittently under load. Where do you investigate first?
• A dependency is slow but not down. How does it affect your service?
• Retry logic increased load and made system worse. Why?
• Traffic spike caused DB overload even though autoscaling worked. What went wrong?
• Some requests succeed, some fail randomly. What could cause this?

⸻

Round 3 – Engineering Thinking (30 min)

• How do you design systems to handle partial failures?
• When do you introduce circuit breakers?
• How do you balance consistency vs availability in real systems?

⸻

💡 Reality

Senior interviews don’t test:

• tools
• commands
• definitions

They test:

• system behavior under load
• failure propagation
• decision making under pressure
